Notes on my thesis

    - three explanantia alone appear to hold any promise of explaining both the safehold (6)
      and the coincidence in which it takes part (7)
                : re `(safehold) (\(6\))` see `^*${2} a ${1}` @ ../20.a_surprising_coincidence.brec
                : re `(coincide)nce.+(\(7\))` see `^*${2} three objects.+${1}` @
                  ../20.a_surprising_coincidence.brec
            • the two design explanantia
                ∵ the coincidence is one of ends and means
            • the explanans of natural cosmogonal selection
                ∵ natural selection figures in the coincidence
        - natural cosmogonal selection is singled out as an outlier among the three
            - by its most promising determination, however, it collapses to mundane design
                : see notepad:2026-10-15e : from natural to artificial by collapse of the former
        - meanwhile the latter is further singled out by another coincidence
            - mundane design’s lineal cosmocrafting inherently endures indefinitely (in aim,
              fit and/or fact) in the face of contingency (existential hazard), like do all
              mechanisms etc. of the threefold coincidence (7)
                : see @ `^*\| a further manifold coincidence$` @ 67.principle.notes.brec
            - its only adequate determinations, however, recall the other two explanantia
                : see notepad:2026-10-15e
                - a choice of reason, a natural telos or God
                    : re `^*- (.+)` see `^*∴ ${same}$` @ `^*∴ a determining motive/impetus to sustain` @
                      67.principle.notes.brec
                    : re `^*- (.+)` see `^*∴ ${same}$` @ `^*∴ .+sources of normativity.+in.+ethics` @
                      `^*• a further threefold coincidence$` @ 67.principle.notes.brec
        - all these coincidences and interconnections hold forth, it seems, a promise of coherence
            - also of equivalence or compatibility among the three explanantia
        - hence my plan
            : join @ 23.plan.notes.brec
        - hence my thesis
            : see notepad:2026-10-18a,d : all promising explanantia lead to the same conclusion
                : cf. @ 80.law.notes.brec
